        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(agents): register session lock helpers in vitest workers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nVitest worker environments do not consistently set `process.env.VITEST` while `session-write-lock.ts` is evaluated. This can skip test-only helper registration and fail compact CI shards before their tests run.\n\nProduction behavior is unchanged. The guard now recognizes the repository's Vitest worker markers: `VITEST_MODE`, `VITEST_POOL_ID`, and `VITEST_WORKER_ID`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact rebased head: `fdfef5a4e3cc987dcb42a17980db8d183dcabee8`\n\n- Formatting, direct lint, and `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Normal and `VITEST_POOL_ID=1` gateway suites both passed: 2 files / 17 tests.\n",
